[[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2892058\">7005R35</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts.</p><p>2. Remove the motor.</p><p>3. Disconnect the electrical connection.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2035567.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[3,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the motor is undamaged,\nand if necessary conduct an electrical test on it.</p><p>Connect the electrical connection.</p><p>Fit the motor and secure with bolts.</p><p><a href=\"#/2892058\">7005R35</a>\n                                           .</p>"]]